ios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.890 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El número de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede ser una decisión técnica o por necesidades específicas. No implica que se hayan violado normas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite se reparten entre distintos proveedores. Verificar si el mismo adjudicatario repite contratos al límite. Analizar si los contratos se concentran en un sector o actividad.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 114 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 23.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.7 to 6.3. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. Contract [1], for 14,890 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [2], for 14,950 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high number of contracts just under the limit does not prove improper conduct. It could reflect market prices, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical indicators alone do not confirm wrongdoing or mismanagement.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts awarded in December to see if they align with other contracts. Review the services provided in contract [1] to ensure they are distinct from other contracts. Look for repeated orders from the same awardee to identify potential patterns.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["xDfKft1jBTZ4zIRvjBVCSw%3D%3D","VJ7EQXL95QY%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D","1uoBeE1DG1CIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}